# Secure Linux (movereset): your desktop look and behaviour. "Reset this computer, keep my files" MOVES these
# aside (never deletes them) into ~/Secure-Linux-old-settings-<date>/ at the next start, before the desktop starts,
# so the desktop starts fresh. "secure-linux-reset undo-settings" puts them back.
# One path per line, relative to the home folder; a folder line covers everything inside it.
# Never listed here: anything in never-touch.list (files, keys, passwords, browsers, messages, app data).
#
# KDE Plasma (full profile): look, panels, widgets, window rules, shortcuts, input, power, screen lock
.config/kdeglobals
.config/kwinrc
.config/kwinrulesrc
.config/kwinoutputconfig.json
.config/plasmarc
.config/plasmashellrc
.config/plasma-org.kde.plasma.desktop-appletsrc
.config/plasma-localerc
.config/plasmanotifyrc
.config/kglobalshortcutsrc
.config/khotkeysrc
.config/kcminputrc
.config/kxkbrc
.config/kscreenlockerrc
.config/ksmserverrc
.config/krunnerrc
.config/kded5rc
.config/kded6rc
.config/powerdevilrc
.config/powermanagementprofilesrc
.config/kactivitymanagerdrc
.config/kactivitymanagerd-statsrc
.config/systemsettingsrc
